WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.609
A stack follows last-in, first-out order.

00:00:02.609 --> 00:00:10.872
The 8085 uses the stack for operations such as saving register pairs and storing return addresses during subroutine calls.

00:00:10.872 --> 00:00:16.960
A valid stack pointer and reserved stack memory are prerequisites for reliable stack operations.

00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:24.245
Save the BC pair before changing it, perform the subroutine work, and restore the pair before returning.

00:00:24.245 --> 00:00:27.573
Every saved value must be restored in reverse order.

00:00:27.573 --> 00:00:30.900
The subroutine must also preserve the call’s return-address discipline.

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:34.288
Which saved pair is popped first?

00:00:34.288 --> 00:00:36.675
The stack uses last-in, first-out order.
